## **2.3 Analytical Outputs (Full Scope)**

The project produces ten distinct analytical outputs. Each is described briefly here and detailed in Section 5.

* **Bottleneck Map:** Service-to-showroom ratio per brand per zone, with severity classification (mild / moderate / severe).
* **Revenue Leakage Estimate:** Monetised estimate of sales lost due to service underinvestment, using FADA retail data and average selling price.
* **Correlation Analysis:** Pearson r coefficient testing whether service center density positively correlates with zone-level sales volume.
* **Expansion Priority Index:** Composite score ranking zones where a brand should open its next service center for maximum impact.
* **Clustering vs. Spread Analysis:** Herfindahl-Hirschman Index applied to service center city-level distribution to detect urban concentration.
* **Brand Maturity vs. Network Balance:** Comparison of sales growth rate against service network growth rate to flag structural capacity risk.
* **Northeast / Hill-State Neglect Score:** Weighted underservice index specific to geographically isolated states.
* **EV Brand Comparison:** Same bottleneck analysis applied to Ola Electric and Ather Energy to demonstrate the forward-looking risk.
* **Competitor Advantage Map:** Cross-brand analysis identifying which competitor is best positioned in each zone where a brand has a bottleneck.
* **Rural vs. Urban Bottleneck Split:** Tier 1 / 2 / 3 city classification applied to service center locations to test whether bottlenecks concentrate in smaller towns.

# **3. Data Sources**

## **3.1 Primary Source — BikeWale Scrape**

BikeWale (bikewale.com) is the primary data source for showroom and service center counts. It aggregates dealer and service data for all major brands across Indian cities and is the most comprehensive publicly accessible source for this purpose.

| **Data Point** | **BikeWale URL Pattern** | **Update Frequency** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Showroom count per city | bikewale.com/dealer-showrooms/{brand}/{city}/ | Weekly |
| Service center count per city | bikewale.com/service-centers/{brand}/{city}/ | Weekly |
| Service center addresses | Extracted from listing page | As updated by brand |
| City / pincode | Listed in each record | Static |

## **3.2 Secondary Source — Brand Official Locators**

Each brand's official dealer/service locator is used to cross-validate BikeWale data and catch any listings not aggregated by third parties.

| **Brand** | **Official Locator URL** |
| --- | --- |
| Royal Enfield | dealers.royalenfield.com/{state} |
| Hero MotoCorp | heromotocorp.com/en-in/locate-us.html |
| Bajaj Auto | bajajauto.com/locate-dealer |
| TVS Motor | tvsmotor.com/dealer-locator |
| Honda (HMSI) | honda2wheelersindia.com/service-network |
| Ola Electric | olaelectric.com/service-centres |
| Ather Energy | atherenergy.com/service-center |

## **3.3 Sales Data — FADA State-wise Retail Reports**

The Federation of Automobile Dealers Associations (FADA) publishes monthly state-wise retail registration data for all two-wheeler brands. This is the standard proxy for regional revenue in the absence of brand-disclosed zone-level financials.

|  |
| --- |
| **Why FADA and not annual reports?**  No Indian two-wheeler brand publicly discloses zone-wise or state-wise revenue breakdowns in their annual reports. National-level revenue is available but cannot be disaggregated by region. FADA retail data is the accepted industry-standard proxy used by analysts, investment firms, and researchers for regional sales performance. |

FADA data is available at fada.in and covers monthly retail (end-customer) registrations — not wholesale dispatches — making it a more accurate proxy for actual demand.

## **3.4 Supplementary Data**

* **India Census population data:** Used for tier 1 / 2 / 3 city classification. Available free from censusindia.gov.in.
* **Average Selling Price (ASP) per brand:** Derived from brand annual reports (revenue divided by units sold). Used to convert unit gaps into rupee revenue leakage estimates.
* **India state shapefile:** Used by GeoPandas for choropleth map rendering. Available from the Survey of India or open GIS repositories.
* **Sales growth rates (historical):** From brand annual reports and FADA historical archives, used for the brand maturity vs. network balance analysis.

